{"id":"word:hebrew:H1715","type":"word","title":"דָּגָן","subtitle":"H1715 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, increase , i.e. grain","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to דָּגָן (H1715) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 40 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"דָּגָן (dâgân) means properly, increase , i.e. grain First listed occurrence: 2Chr 31 5."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"דָּגָן","transliteration":"dâgân","pronunciation":"daw-gawn'","strong":"H1715","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1715","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["דָּגָן֙","הַ/דָּגָן֙","דָגָ֖ן","דָּגָ֖ן","דְּגָֽנְ/ךָ֙"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",17],["HTd/Ncmsa",8],["HNcmsc/Sp2ms",5],["HC/Ncmsa",3],["HNcmsc/Sp3mp",2],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",1],["HNcmsc/Sp2fs",1],["HC/Td/Ncmsa",1],["HRd/Ncmsa",1],["HC/Ncmsc",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, increase , i.e. grain","usage":"corn (floor), wheat.","full":"H1715. dagan דָּגָן noun masculine corn, grain (of cereals) (Late Hebrew id. , Samaritan see Thes.; compare Phoenician דגן ארצת ) — דָּגָן Gen 27:28-29 t.; construct דְּגַן Psa 78:24 ; suffix דְּגָנִי Hosea 2:11 , דְּגָָֽנְךָ Deut 7:13 ; 12:17 ; 14:23 ; 18:4 , דְּגָנֶ֑ךָ 11:14 , דְּגָנֵךְ Isa 62:8 , דְּגָנָם Psa 4:8 ; 65:10 — corn , with תִּירוֺשׁ must , q. v., Gen 27:28 , 37 (both J) Psa 4:8 ; Isa 62:8 ; Hosea 2:11 ; 7:14 ; 9:1 ; Zech 9:17 ; compare also Num 18:27 (P; here, for מִןהַֿיָּ֑קֶב מְלֵאָה תירושׁ, ), Lam 2:12 (where יַיִן ), Hosea 14:8 (where גֶּפֶן & יֵין לְבָנוֺן ); ותירושׁ דגן ארץ of land of Canaan Deut 33:28 ; of land of captives (words of the Rabshak) 2Kin 18:32 = Isa 36:17 (other products, also, named in both); usually with תירושׁ & יצהר Num 18:12 ; Deut 7:13 ; 11:14 ; 12:17 ; 14:23 ; 18:4 ; 28:51 ; 2Chr 31:5 (+ דבשׁ ) 32:28 ; Neh 5:11 ; Nehemiah 10:40; 13:5 , 12 ; Jer 31:12 ; Hosea 2:10 ; Hosea 2:24; Joel 1:10 ; 2:19 ; Hag 1:11 ; also Joel 1:17 Me; (compa